# Registers and regular expressions from the softcode audit (#2268): letq() keeps only the registers
# it names, strmatch() fills the registers it is given, and patterns take PCRE's POSIX classes and
# Python-style named groups.
::case rra.login
::login wiz Wiz wizpass
think ok

::case rra.letq  a register letq() did not name is the caller's
think [setr(B,1)][letq(A,2,setr(B,2))]:%qB
think [setq(C,1)][letq(A,2,unsetq(C))]:[r(C)]:[letq(A,add(1,1),%qA)]

::case rra.strmatch  the registers named in the third argument take the captures
think [strmatch(foo:bar,*:*,0 1)]/%q0/%q1
think [strmatch(abc,?b?,- x)]/%qx|[strmatch(nope,*:*,0 1)]

::case rra.posix  POSIX classes inside a bracket expression
think [regmatch(a,\[\[:alnum:\]\])] [regmatch(%b,^\[\[:space:\]\]$)] [regmatch(G,^\[\[:xdigit:\]\]$)] [regmatch(f,^\[^\[:digit:\]\]$)]

::case rra.named  Python-style named groups
think [regedit(best,(?P<c>.)est,$<c>R)] [regmatch(abab,^(?P<x>ab)(?P=x)$)]
